<name>CAN Communication</name>
<ttl id="10033_S0007_741KB_T000K" variety="T000K">
<name>CAN Communication System</name>
<para id="RM000002087005X" category="J" type-id="801QW" name-id="950V3-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Accessory Gateway Communication Stop Mode</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000002087005X_01" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00000EX00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" align="center" colwidth="1.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Diagnosis Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Symptom</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Suspected Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Accessory Gateway Communication Stop Mode</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>"Accessory Gateway" is not displayed on the "CAN Bus Connected ECU Check" screen of TaSCAN (w/ remote engine starter/dealer option)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Certification ECU outputs B2779 "Engine Starter Communication Error" (w/ remote engine starter/dealer option)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Accessory bus buffer branch line open or connector malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Accessory bus buffer GND malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Dealer-installed option power source malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Dealer-installed option internal malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002087005X_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00000EY00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B162441J01" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002087005X_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00000EZ00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>When measuring the resistance of the CAN bus, turn the ignition switch off, check that warning functions such as the key reminder warning system are not operating, and leave the vehicle for at least 1 minutes without operating the key or switches or opening and closing the doors before starting the measurement. If it is necessary to open a door during inspection, open it beforehand.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When inspecting each connector, before disconnecting it, push the connector case in the connecting direction and check that the connector is not loose or disconnected.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When disconnecting a connector, check that the connector terminals and connector case are free of damage, deformation, corrosion, etc.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002087005X_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000002087005X_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00000F000000">
<testtitle>CAN Bus Open Circuit Inspection (Accessory Bus Buffer)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the IG OFF and disconnect the accessory bus buffer connector from the dealer-installed option.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of the accessory bus buffer connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C129976J08" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.93in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.07in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1(CAN+) - 2(CAN-)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>54 to 69Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002087005X_04_0002" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000002087005X_04_0004" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002087005X_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___00000F100000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness (GND)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), inspect the resistance between the accessory bus buffer connector terminal and body ground.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C129976J09" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.03in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.14in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>3 (GND) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If there is no malfunction in the vehicle wire harness, check the power source circuit and parts of the installed item for malfunctions, referring to the installation instructions of the dealer-installed option.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002087005X_04_0003" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000002087005X_04_0005" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002087005X_04_0003">
<testtitle>Optional Equipment Check</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002087005X_04_0004">
<testtitle>Repair or replace accessory bus buffer branch line or connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002087005X_04_0005">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Wire Harness or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
